{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["גר ותושב אנכי — I came from a foreign land to sojourn here and I have settled among you; therefore I have no ancestral burial place here." "תנו לי אחוזת קבר — Let me acquire land here, and you, the inhabitants of the city, consent to allow me to bury my dead in it. For a burial holding can exist only with the consent of all the city's inhabitants. And so the text proves before us: when Avraham gave the silver to Ephron and it was confirmed to Avraham as a purchase, only afterward did Avraham bury, and it became his as a burial holding from all the children of Heth." "מלפני — I will take him from before me to bury him."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:44:49.254044355Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}